{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EeneWkRtYqJXMVGEfxAbZD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Per-repo task for the v3 fresh-repo eval\n2\t\n3\tYou are given one repository, `<name>`, from `eval/v3/REPOS.json`. Paths are under `R = ~/code/router-migrate`:\n4\t- `R/eval/work/v3/pristine/<name>`: a clone at the pinned commit. **Read-only:** never modify it.\n5\t- `R/eval/work/v3/base/<name>`: a copy at the same commit. Install dependencies here (`$SRC` in recipe commands).\n6\t- `R/eval/work/v3/envs/<name>`: put the Python virtualenv here (`$ENV`; `$PY` is `$ENV/bin/python`).\n7\t\n8\tDo the two parts below **in this order**. Part A must not be influenced by the tool being evaluated:\n9\t- Never read anything under `R/router_migrate/` except the two catalog files named in `R/eval/heldout/RUBRIC.md`.\n10\t- Never read `R/eval/logs/`, `R/eval/heldout/logs/`, any `.router-migrate/` directory, or other repos' inventories.\n11\t- Never run `router-migrate` / `bin/router-migrate`.\n12\t\n13\t## Hard rules\n14\t- Install only inside `R`; nothing global. Always `source R/scripts/env.sh` first: it pins the uv, npm and pip caches and the uv\n15\t  Pythons into `R/.tools`.\n16\t  - **Python:** `R/.venv/bin/uv venv --python 3.11|3.12 \"$ENV\"`, then `R/.venv/bin/uv pip install --python \"$ENV/bin/python\" ...`\n17\t    with `--exclude-newer 2026-10-13T00:00:00Z`.\n18\t  - **Node:** use `npm` with the cache from env.sh, or the local pnpm/yarn at `R/.tools/pm/node_modules/.bin/{pnpm,yarn}` with\n19\t    `npm_config_store_dir=\"$R/.tools/pnpm-store\"`. Never `npm -g`, `corepack enable`, brew or curl-pipe installers.\n20\t- **No API keys.** Run everything with `RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY` unset (`env -u RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY`). Never call any LLM API; tests must\n21\t  run offline, and when a test hits the network, deselect it and say so.\n22\t- Don't commit anything. Don't touch other repos' directories.\n23\t- Other agents run at the same time. Put any scratch files in a directory named after your repo, e.g.\n24\t  `<scratchpad>/<name>/`, never in a shared path.\n25\t- **Timebox Part B to about 40 minutes.** If the suite can't run offline in that time, record why. A TS repo can fall back to a strict\n26\t  typecheck.\n27\t\n28\t## Part A: blind inventory\n29\tFollow `R/eval/heldout/RUBRIC.md` exactly, reading the pristine copy. Write `R/eval/v3/inventory/<name>.json`.\n30\t- Be exhaustive for production code.\n31\t- Include non-production sites with `\"prod\": false` / `\"expected\": \"nonprod\"`.\n32\t- Use the line where the call or construction expression starts.\n33\t\n34\t## Part B: test recipe\n35\tWrite `R/eval/v3/recipes/<name>.json` in the same shape as the dev-set recipes; read `R/eval/recipes/swarm.json` (Python) and\n36\t`R/eval/recipes/aicommits.json` (TS) as examples. Fields:\n37\t- `name`, `lang` (`py`|`ts`), `python` (Python repos), `pm` (TS repos);\n38\t- `setup`: shell commands that create `$ENV` and install dependencies into `$SRC`. They run from `R` with `$SRC`, `$ENV`, `$PY` and\n39\t  `$RM` (= `R`) substituted. Start each one with `. scripts/env.sh && ...`.\n40\t  - If a Python package is installed editable from `$SRC` (`-e \"$SRC\"`), the eval re-points it at its working copy automatically.\n41\t  - Otherwise set `reinstall`: a list of commands that make `$PY` import the code from `$SRC` (for example a `.pth` file), or rely\n42\t    on running tests with `PYTHONPATH=.`.\n43\t- `test_cmd`: the offline test command, run with cwd = the repo copy. Use `$PY` for Python, and sandbox `HOME`/`TMPDIR` into `$ENV`\n44\t  as the examples do. Pick the repo's own CI test command where possible.\n45\t- `test_env`, `timeout_s`, and `test_kind` (`unit`, or `typecheck` when there are no runnable tests).\n46\t- `baseline`: `{passed, failed, errors, skipped, seconds, exit}` from a real run. Run the command twice and confirm identical counts.\n47\t  - The counts must be what `R/router_migrate/verify.py`'s `parse_counts` reads from the output. You may import and call that one\n48\t    function (`cd R && .venv/bin/python -c \"from router_migrate.verify import parse_counts; ...\"`) to check your output is parsed.\n49\t  - If nothing can run, use `{\"exit\": null, \"reason\": \"...\"}`.\n50\t- TS repos: also `typecheck_cmd` (e.g. `./node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit -p .`) and `typecheck_baseline: {exit, errors}`, with\n51\t  `errors` = the count of `error TS` in the output. Pre-existing errors are fine; just record them.\n52\t- `notes`: what you chose and why, anything deselected, Node/Python versions.\n53\t\n54\tRun the setup and tests in `base/<name>` (`$SRC` = base).\n55\t\n56\tWhen done, reply with:\n57\t- the inventory totals (prod sites by expected outcome);\n58\t- the recipe's test command and baseline counts (or why there are none);\n59\t- anything unusual, such as rubric cases you weren't sure how to classify.\n60\t\n61\t## v3 additions\n62\t- The rubric is `R/eval/heldout/RUBRIC.md`; ignore the output path it names and write to `R/eval/v3/inventory/<name>.json`.\n63\t- Also never read `R/eval/v3/runs/`, `R/eval/v3/results.json` or `R/router_migrate/prompts/`.\n64\t- **Repos with no test suite:** write a smoke `test_cmd` that proves the code still imports and compiles, so a migration that\n65\t  breaks an import is caught. Python: install the deps, then `$PY -m compileall -q <package dirs>` plus a short\n66\t  `$PY -c \"import <each production module that contains an LLM call>\"` with dummy env vars (e.g. `OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-dummy`)\n67\t  so module import side effects don't fail; print a final line `N passed in Xs` (pytest style) so `parse_counts` reads it.\n68\t  TS: `typecheck_cmd` plus `test_kind: \"typecheck\"`. Record exactly what the smoke command checks in `notes`.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4af49a4b-c14f-41cf-83cf-bdddab83488a","uuid":"2dc3d493-a90b-49f7-83cb-2e5a55093504","timestamp":"2026-10-14T16:56:16.686Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sanjithsambath/code/router-migrate-v4/eval/v3/AGENT_TASK.md","content":"# Per-repo task for the v3 fresh-repo eval\n\nYou are given one repository, `<name>`, from `eval/v3/REPOS.json`. Paths are under `R = ~/code/router-migrate`:\n- `R/eval/work/v3/pristine/<name>`: a clone at the pinned commit. **Read-only:** never modify it.\n- `R/eval/work/v3/base/<name>`: a copy at the same commit. Install dependencies here (`$SRC` in recipe commands).\n- `R/eval/work/v3/envs/<name>`: put the Python virtualenv here (`$ENV`; `$PY` is `$ENV/bin/python`).\n\nDo the two parts below **in this order**. Part A must not be influenced by the tool being evaluated:\n- Never read anything under `R/router_migrate/` except the two catalog files named in `R/eval/heldout/RUBRIC.md`.\n- Never read `R/eval/logs/`, `R/eval/heldout/logs/`, any `.router-migrate/` directory, or other repos' inventories.\n- Never run `router-migrate` / `bin/router-migrate`.\n\n## Hard rules\n- Install only inside `R`; nothing global. Always `source R/scripts/env.sh` first: it pins the uv, npm and pip caches and the uv\n  Pythons into `R/.tools`.\n  - **Python:** `R/.venv/bin/uv venv --python 3.11|3.12 \"$ENV\"`, then `R/.venv/bin/uv pip install --python \"$ENV/bin/python\" ...`\n    with `--exclude-newer 2026-10-13T00:00:00Z`.\n  - **Node:** use `npm` with the cache from env.sh, or the local pnpm/yarn at `R/.tools/pm/node_modules/.bin/{pnpm,yarn}` with\n    `npm_config_store_dir=\"$R/.tools/pnpm-store\"`. Never `npm -g`, `corepack enable`, brew or curl-pipe installers.\n- **No API keys.** Run everything with `RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY` unset (`env -u RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY`). Never call any LLM API; tests must\n  run offline, and when a test hits the network, deselect it and say so.\n- Don't commit anything. Don't touch other repos' directories.\n- Other agents run at the same time. Put any scratch files in a directory named after your repo, e.g.\n  `<scratchpad>/<name>/`, never in a shared