{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KibbVBMTZ81gECxMXAwYA5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Held-out inventory rubric\n2\t\n3\tYour job: inventory every LLM API call site in a repository and record what *should* happen to it in a migration onto Ramp's Router.\n4\tWork from the repository's source only.\n5\t- Do **not** read anything under `~/code/router-migrate/router_migrate/`, `eval/logs/` or `eval/heldout/logs/`, and never look at a\n6\t  `.router-migrate/` directory: this inventory must be independent of the tool being evaluated.\n7\t- You may read the Router model catalog (`~/code/router-migrate/router_migrate/data/catalog.json`, ids under `models`) and the measured\n8\t  dated-id equivalences (`router_migrate/data/dated_equivalents.json`). Those are facts about Router, not about the tool.\n9\t\n10\t## What Router is (measured facts)\n11\tRouter serves exactly three endpoints:\n12\t- `GET /v1/models`;\n13\t- `POST /v1/responses` (OpenAI Responses API);\n14\t- `POST /v1/messages` and `/v1/messages/count_tokens` (Anthropic Messages API).\n15\t\n16\tThere is no chat-completions, embeddings, images, audio, files, assistants, vector-store, moderation or legacy-completions endpoint.\n17\t\n18\tHow Router treats requests:\n19\t- It serves only the model ids in the catalog (plus the listed dated equivalences); any other model id is 404.\n20\t- It keeps no server-side state: `store: true` returns 400; `previous_response_id`, `conversation` and `responses.retrieve` don't work.\n21\t- It uses one Router API key per deployment, with no per-user keys.\n22\t\n23\t## What counts as one site (counting unit)\n24\t- **Direct SDK call:** one site per expression. This covers `client.chat.completions.create/parse/stream`,\n25\t  `client.responses.create/stream/parse/retrieve`, `client.messages.create/stream/count_tokens`, `client.beta.messages.*`,\n26\t  `client.embeddings.create`, `client.images.*`, `client.audio.*`, `client.files.*`, `client.beta.assistants|threads.*`,\n27\t  `client.vector_stores.*`, `client.models.list` and `client.completions.create`.\n28\t  - A bound reference counts too (`create = client.chat.completions.create`).\n29\t- **LangChain / LlamaIndex:** one site per *chat-model or embeddings construction* (`ChatOpenAI(...)`, `ChatAnthropic(...)`,\n30\t  `OpenAIEmbeddings(...)`, llama_index `OpenAI(...)`). Do not count `.invoke()` / `.stream()` calls separately.\n31\t- **Vercel AI SDK:** one site per `generateText` / `streamText` / `generateObject` / `streamObject` / `embed` / `embedMany` call.\n32\t  Provider constructions (`createOpenAI(...)`, the default `openai` provider) are *not* sites when calls exist.\n33\t- **LiteLLM:** one site per `completion` / `acompletion` / `embedding` call.\n34\t- **Other vendor SDKs:** one site per generation call, e.g. `google.genai`, `mistralai`, `cohere`, `groq`, `ollama`, `boto3`\n35\t  bedrock-runtime `invoke_model` / `converse`.\n36\t- **Raw HTTP:** one site per request (`requests`/`httpx`/`fetch`/`axios`) to `api.openai.com` or `api.anthropic.com` generation\n37\t  endpoints. Also count raw HTTP to other LLM vendors' endpoints.\n38\t- **prod:** set `prod: false` for tests, examples, demos, notebooks, eval/benchmark harnesses, docs, scripts not part of the shipped\n39\t  app, and vendored third-party code. Inventory them anyway.\n40\t\n41\t## Expected outcome per production site (apply in this order)\n42\t1. **kept**: the surface has no Router endpoint: embeddings, images, audio, files, assistants/threads, vector stores, moderation,\n43\t   legacy completions, realtime.\n44\t2. **kept**: the request goes to another vendor's endpoint. That covers a `base_url`/`baseURL` to a non-OpenAI/Anthropic host\n45\t   (Groq, DeepSeek, OpenRouter, Together, Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, a local server...), Azure OpenAI, Bedrock and Vertex, and\n46\t   also a base URL chosen from a user-defined object at runtime. Moving these would change vendor and model.\n47\t3. **kept**: stateful Responses use on that client (`previous_response_id`, `conversation`, `store=True`, `retrieve`/`input_items`),\n48\t   or `file_search` with vector store ids / `code_interpreter` with file ids.\n49\t4. **flagged**: the API key is per user or tenant, i.e. it comes from a request, user, profile or session object, or a per-call\n50\t   function parameter fed from one. Env vars or app config do not count.\n51\t5. **flagged**: the call sends Anthropic beta features (`betas=`, `anthropic-beta` header, `client.beta.messages`).\n52\t6. **flagged**: the model is a literal (or a constant) that is not a Router catalog id or listed dated equivalence. Also flagged:\n53\t   the model is chosen at runtime and *none* of the repo's model-name literals for that provider family are in the catalog.\n54\t7. **handoff**: another gateway (Vercel AI Gateway, Cloudflare AI gateway...), raw HTTP to api.openai.com / api.anthropic.com\n55\t   generation endpoints, or another vendor's SDK where a model it uses is in Router's catalog (e.g. a `google.genai` call with a\n56\t   Gemini model id that is in the catalog).\n57\t8. **migrated**: everything else on OpenAI chat-completions/responses or Anthropic messages (directly or via LangChain, LlamaIndex,\n58\t   the AI SDK or LiteLLM) that uses the vendor's default endpoint. That includes an endpoint taken from env/config that defaults to\n59\t   the vendor, with the operator's key, and a model that is a catalog id or chosen at runtime.\n60\t\n61\t## Output\n62\tWrite JSON to `~/code/router-migrate/eval/heldout/inventory/<name>.json`:\n63\t```json\n64\t{\"repo\": \"owner/name\", \"commit\": \"<sha>\", \"sites\": [\n65\t  {\"file\": \"path/from/repo/root.py\", \"line\": 42, \"prod\": true, \"sdk\": \"openai|anthropic|langchain-openai|langchain-anthropic|vercel-ai|llamaindex|litellm|google-genai|raw-http|other:<name>\",\n66\t   \"surface\": \"chat|responses|messages|embeddings|images|audio|files|assistants|vector_stores|models|completions|other\",\n67\t   \"endpoint\": \"default|env-config|other:<host or vendor>|azure|bedrock|vertex|gateway:<name>|runtime-user-defined|unknown\",\n68\t   \"key_source\": \"env|config|per-user|literal|none|unknown\", \"model\": {\"value\": \"gpt-4o-mini or null\", \"static\": true},\n69\t   \"beta\": false, \"stateful_responses\": false, \"expected\": \"migrated|kept|flagged|handoff|nonprod\", \"why\": \"<short reason, citing the rule number>\"}\n70\t]}\n71\t```\n72\tUse the line of the call expression or construction, i.e. where `create(`, `ChatOpenAI(`, `generateText(` or `fetch(` starts.\n73\tUse `expected: \"nonprod\"` for non-production sites.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4af49a4b-c14f-41cf-83cf-bdddab83488a","uuid":"6a2377cb-a992-4a7f-96c0-a378ebb490af","timestamp":"2026-10-14T16:56:17.344Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sanjithsambath/code/router-migrate-v4/eval/heldout/RUBRIC.md","content":"# Held-out inventory rubric\n\nYour job: inventory every LLM API call site in a repository and record what *should* happen to it in a migration onto Ramp's Router.\nWork from the repository's source only.\n- Do **not** read anything under `~/code/router-migrate/router_migrate/`, `eval/logs/` or `eval/heldout/logs/`, and never look at a\n  `.router-migrate/` directory: this inventory must be independent of the tool being evaluated.\n- You may read the Router model catalog (`~/code/router-migrate/router_migrate/data/catalog.json`, ids under `models`) and the measured\n  dated-id equivalences (`router_migrate/data/dated_equivalents.json`). Those are facts about Router, not about the tool.\n\n## What Router is (measured facts)\nRouter serves exactly three endpoints:\n- `GET /v1/models`;\n- `POST /v1/responses` (OpenAI Responses API);\n- `POST /v1/messages` and `/v1/messages/count_tokens` (Anthropic Messages API).\n\nThere is no chat-completions, embeddings, images, audio, files, assistants, vector-store, moderation or legacy-completions endpoint.\n\nHow Router treats requests:\n- It serves only the model ids in the catalog (plus the listed dated equivalences); any other model id is 404.\n- It keeps no server-side state: `store: true` returns 400; `previous_response_id`, `conversation` and `responses.retrieve` don't work.\n- It uses one Router API key per deployment, with no per-user keys.\n\n## What counts as one site (counting unit)\n- **Direct SDK call:** one site per expression. This covers `client.chat.completions.create/parse/stream`,\n  `client.responses.create/stream/parse/retrieve`, `client.messages.create/stream/count_tokens`, `client.beta.messages.*`,\n  `client.embeddings.create`, `client.images.*`, `client.audio.*`, `client.files.*`, `client.beta.assistants|threads.*`,\n  `client.vector_stores.*`, `client.models.list` and `client.completions.create`.\n  - A bound reference counts too (`create = client.chat.completions.create`).\n- **LangChain / LlamaIndex:** one site per *chat-model or embeddings construction* (`ChatOpenAI(...)`, `ChatAnthropic(...)`,\n  `OpenAIEmbeddings(...)`, llama_index `OpenAI(...)`). Do not count `.invoke()` / `.stream()` calls separately.\n- **Vercel AI SDK:** one site per `generateText` / `streamText` / `generateObject` / `streamObject` / `embed` / `embedMany` call.\n  Provider constructions (`createOpenAI(...)`, the default `openai` provider) are *not* sites when calls exist.\n- **LiteLLM:** one site per `completion` / `acompletion` / `embedding` call.\n- **Other vendor SDKs:** one site per generation call, e.g. `google.genai`, `mistralai`, `cohere`, `groq`, `ollama`, `boto3`\n  bedrock-runtime `invoke_model` / `converse`.\n- **Raw HTTP:** one site per request (`requests`/`httpx`/`fetch`/`axios`) to `api.openai.com` or `api.anthropic.com` generation\n  endpoints. Also count raw HTTP to other LLM vendors' endpoints.\n- **prod:** set `prod: false` for tests, examples, demos, notebooks, eval/benchmark harnesses, docs, scripts not part of the shipped\n  app, and vendored third-party code. Inventory them anyway.\n\n## Expected outcome per production site (apply in this order)\n1. **kept**: the surface has no Router endpoint: embeddings, images, audio, files, assistants/threads, vector stores, moderation,\n   legacy completions, realtime.\n2. **kept**: the request goes to another vendor's endpoint. That covers a `base_url`/`baseURL` to a non-OpenAI/Anthropic host\n   (Groq, DeepSeek, OpenRouter, Together, Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, a local server...), Azure OpenAI, Bedrock and Vertex, and\n   also a base URL chosen from a user-defined object at runtime. Moving these would change vendor and model.\n3. **kept**: stateful Responses use on that client (`previous_response_id`, `conversation`, `store=True`, `retrieve`/`input_items`),\n   or `file_search` with vector store ids / `code_interpreter` with file ids.\n4. **flagged**: the API key is per user or tenant, i.e. it comes from a request, user, profile or session object, or a per-call\n   function parameter fed from one. Env vars or app config do not count.\n5. **flagged**: the call sends Anthropic beta features (`betas=`, `anthropic-beta` header, `client.beta.messages`).\n6. **flagged**: the model is a literal (or a constant) that is not a Router catalog id or listed dated equivalence. Also flagged:\n   the model is chosen at runtime and *none* of the repo's model-name literals for that provider family are in the catalog.\n7. **handoff**: another gateway (Vercel AI Gateway, Cloudflare AI gateway...), raw HTTP to api.openai.com / api.anthropic.com\n   generation endpoints, or another vendor's SDK where a model it uses is in Router's catalog (e.g. a `google.genai` call with a\n   Gemini model id that is in the catalog).\n8. **migrated**: everything else on OpenAI chat-completions/responses or Anthropic messages (directly or via LangChain, LlamaIndex,\n   the AI SDK or LiteLLM) that uses the vendor's default endpoint. That includes an endpoint taken from env/config that defaults to\n   the vendor, with the operator's key, and a model that is a catalog id or chosen at runtime.\n\n## Output\nWrite JSON to `~/code/router-migrate/eval/heldout/inventory/<name>.json`:\n```json\n{\"repo\": \"owner/name\", \"commit\": \"<sha>\", \"sites\": [\n  {\"file\": \"path/from/repo/root.py\", \"line\": 42, \"prod\": true, \"sdk\": \"openai|anthropic|langchain-openai|langchain-anthropic|vercel-ai|llamaindex|litellm|google-genai|raw-http|other:<name>\",\n   \"surface\": \"chat|responses|messages|embeddings|images|audio|files|assistants|vector_stores|models|completions|other\",\n   \"endpoint\": \"default|env-config|other:<host or vendor>|azure|bedrock|vertex|gateway:<name>|runtime-user-defined|unknown\",\n   \"key_source\": \"env|config|per-user|literal|none|unknown\", \"model\": {\"value\": \"gpt-4o-mini or null\", \"static\": true},\n   \"beta\": false, \"stateful_responses\": false, \"expected\": \"migrated|kept|flagged|handoff|nonprod\", \"why\": \"<short reason, citing the rule number>\"}\n]}\n```\nUse the line of the call expression or construction, i.e. where `create(`, `ChatOpenAI(`, `generateText(` or `fetch(` starts.\nUse `expected: \"nonprod\"` for non-production sites.\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
